---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Job Placement
description: Hands-on support from resume to signed offer — matching, coaching, and negotiation help for candidates who want a job placed, not just applications sent.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
  - /assets/js/candidate-route.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   JOB PLACEMENT — creative redesign (see claude_helper/JOB-PLACEMENT-PAGE.md).

   Same information architecture as the pilot pass:
     Hero → Bridge → Included → What changes → Process → FAQ → CTA
   What changed is how the sections occupy the screen. One recurring device runs
   through the page — THE CANDIDATE ROUTE (partials/candidate-route.njk):
   START → PROFILE → MATCH → INTERVIEW → OFFER. It is drawn incomplete in the hero
   and resolves at the CTA; candidate-route.js lights further nodes on scroll.

   Discipline unchanged: stats, the success story, candidate voices and the
   employer wall stay gated until real, consented content exists. See the TODOs.
   ================================================================ #}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "Job Placement" }] %}
{% set routeNodes = [
  { label: "Start" }, { label: "Profile" }, { label: "Match" },
  { label: "Interview" }, { label: "Offer" }
] %}

{# ---------- 1. Hero — 12-column editorial composition ----------
   The fee answer ($0) is a marker on the photo, not small print. The candidate
   route starts here, deliberately incomplete. ---------- #}
<section data-route-step="1" class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pr-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">A named recruiter, start to finish</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
          Get placed,<br>not just applied.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-6 max-w-xl">
          A named recruiter works your search end to end — resume, matching,
          interview prep, and negotiation — because a job search shouldn't be
          something you do alone.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}" class="btn-primary">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Start your job search
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            See all services {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
          </a>
        </div>

        {# The recurring device, drawn at its first node. #}
        {% set routeActive = 1 %}
        {% set routeProgress = true %}
        <div class="mt-12 max-w-lg">
          {% include "partials/candidate-route.njk" %}
        </div>

        {# TODO — confirm every figure with the client before launch (stats.json).
           Candidate-facing order: success rate last, partner count dropped. #}
        {% set heroStats = [] %}
        {% for s in stats.list %}
          {% if s.label != "Partner Companies" %}{% set _ = heroStats.push(s) %}{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        <dl class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-12 gap-y-5 border-t border-ink/12 pt-6">
          {% for stat in heroStats.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["job-placement"].cover %}
        <figure class="jp-frame">
          <span class="jp-frame-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div class="jp-frame-media jp-reveal">
            <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
                 alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
                 width="1400" height="1750" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
                 class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover">
          </div>
          <figcaption class="jp-frame-caption">The first conversation</figcaption>

          {# Frost — it floats over the photograph (THEME.md §3). #}
          <div class="glass-frost jp-fee">
            <p class="meta">Cost to you</p>
            <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">$0</p>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# TODO — Employer wall gated. placed-at.njk hotlinks logo.clearbit.com for
   Amazon / Microsoft / Accenture etc. — a client list we can't substantiate.
   Re-enable only with a real, permitted set of employer names.
{% include "partials/placed-at.njk" %}
#}

{# ---------- 2. The bridge — application becomes a conversation ----------
   Deliberately short: a breath between the hero and the feature list. ---------- #}
<section class="border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-14 sm:py-20">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-baseline lg:gap-12">
      <p class="eyebrow lg:col-span-3">The difference</p>
      <div class="lg:col-span-9">
        <p class="assertion text-2xl sm:text-3xl">Your application should go somewhere.</p>
        <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-xl">
          With a named recruiter behind it, your search has context, follow-up, and
          a person accountable for what happens next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 3. What's included — vertical editorial index ----------
   Sticky heading on lg, the six items scroll past; the reader's current item
   takes the route node. ---------- #}
<section id="included" data-route-step="2" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set included = [
    { icon: "check", t: "Resume & profile optimization", d: "We rebuild your resume and profile around what actually gets noticed." },
    { icon: "users", t: "Interview coaching", d: "Mock interviews and real feedback before it counts." },
    { icon: "target", t: "Employer matching", d: "We only put you in front of roles that fit your background and goals." },
    { icon: "chart", t: "Offer negotiation support", d: "We help you evaluate and negotiate before you sign anything." },
    { icon: "clock", t: "Post-placement check-in", d: "We follow up at 30 and 90 days to make sure it's working out." },
    { icon: "briefcase", t: "Application tracking", d: "One recruiter, one thread — no chasing status across job boards." }
  ] %}

  <div class="grid gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-[17rem_1fr] lg:gap-x-16">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <h2 class="section-title">Six things you get, from day one.</h2>
      <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
        Support at every stage of the search, not just a stack of applications sent
        on your behalf.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="jp-index" data-jp-index>
      {% for item in included %}
      <li class="jp-index-row" data-jp-item>
        <div class="jp-index-head">
          <span class="jp-index-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <span class="jp-index-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="jp-index-icon">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-3">{{ item.t }}</h3>
        <p class="body-copy mt-1.5">{{ item.d }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <p class="jp-note mt-14 max-w-2xl">
    No guarantee of an offer, and no promise on timeline — but if a placement
    doesn't work out inside 90 days, we re-open your search at no additional cost.
  </p>
</section>

{# ---------- 4. What changes — uncertainty becoming a route ----------
   Each row draws its link to a filled node as it enters view. ---------- #}
<section id="changes" data-route-step="3" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    {% set contrasts = [
      { a: "Applications into a void, no reply", b: "A named recruiter who tells you where each one stands" },
      { a: "No idea why you were passed over", b: "Feedback after every interview" },
      { a: "Competing with hundreds of applicants", b: "Introduced to employers already expecting your resume" },
      { a: "Guessing what the interview will cover", b: "Prepped for the specific team you're meeting" }
    ] %}

    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="assertion sm:text-3xl">
        On your own, an application goes into a void. With us, it goes to
        someone already expecting it.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12" data-jp-split>
      <div class="jp-change-head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>On your own</span>
        <span></span>
        <span class="text-brand">With us</span>
      </div>
      <ul>
        {% for row in contrasts %}
        <li class="jp-change" data-jp-row>
          <span class="jp-change-old">{{ row.a }}</span>
          <span class="jp-change-link" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="jp-change-new">{{ row.b }}</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 5. The process — a horizontal journey map (vertical route on mobile).
   Genuinely ordinal; the node the reader is level with is the current step,
   earlier nodes read as completed. Durations and copy unchanged. ---------- #}
<section id="procedure" data-route-step="4" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set steps = [
    { label: "Consultation", duration: "30 minutes", description: "A conversation about where you are and where you want to go." },
    { label: "Profile build", duration: "3–5 days", description: "Resume, profile, and positioning built around your target roles." },
    { label: "Matching", duration: "Ongoing", description: "Introductions only to employers that fit — no mass applications." },
    { label: "Interviews", duration: "", description: "Coaching before every conversation that matters." },
    { label: "Offer", duration: "", description: "Negotiation support and a check-in once you've started." }
  ] %}
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h2 class="section-title mt-2">Five steps to an offer.</h2>
  </div>

  <ol class="jp-journey mt-14" data-jp-journey>
    {% for step in steps %}
    <li class="jp-journey-step{% if loop.first %} is-current{% endif %}" data-jp-node>
      <span class="jp-journey-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
      <span class="jp-journey-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="jp-journey-label">{{ step.label }}</p>
      <p class="jp-journey-meta">{{ step.duration or "—" }}</p>
      <p class="jp-journey-desc">{{ step.description }}</p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

